srow(165, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'OR GO THIS WAY: WE REASON A THING THAT APPLIES TO MANY AND FEW FROM A THING THAT APPLIES TO MANY AND FEW; LET THE FIRST FLEECE NOT PROVE, WHICH APPLIES ONLY TO MANY. ({SP_(165, 8, "ואל", "יוכיח", "ראשית", "הגז")} "and let the first fleece not prove"; {SP_(165, 8, "אלא", "במרבה")} "only to many"): the counter-analogy (the fleece needs five sheep — 166:8) — the reasoning tied (the row without a citation). Fresh.')
